                <pb facs="0212" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4142: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-24T23:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24, 1919,
                                11 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 24, 10:03
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1316. Your 1067, March 11th, 6 p.m. Commission has given careful consideration to
                    Vice Consul Imbrie’s report, but feels that the relief of
                    Petrograd and other cities of Russia is too large an undertaking for any Red
                    Cross organization or group of organizations. Commission doubts whether at
                    present time the American Government should take the initiative and also if it
                    has funds available to undertake measures on an adequate scale and feels further
                    that any relief for Russia should be part of a definite inter-Allied program.
                    Since Commission favors in theory and practice [<hi rendition="#italic">any
                        practicable</hi>] humanitarian measures for the Russian civilian population
                    in all sections, Mr. Hoover’s opinion is
                    being sought and Commission will welcome any further suggestions which may occur
                    to the Department.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
